    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass and the build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July) across the `POST /api/owners` pipeline and the owner read model.\n\n**New helper \u2014 `FiscalYears`** (`rest/function/common/FiscalYears.java`)\n- `yearOf(date)` \u2014 the four-digit fiscal year a date falls in (month \u2265 July \u2192 next calendar year).\n- `labelOf(owner)` \u2014 the `'FY<YY>'` label from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` (`null` when no date).\n- `elapsedSinceRegistration(owner)` \u2014 fiscal years elapsed since registration, for tenure.\n\n**`fiscalYear` response field**\n- Added the `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`, so it appears on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n- Wired it in `OwnerMapper` via `FiscalYears.labelOf(owner)` (added the import and `imports=` entry).\n\n**Membership identifier** \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber` now derives the `-M<YY>` segment from `FiscalYears.yearOf(registrationDate)` instead of the calendar year, so it matches the returned `fiscalYear` (Cp14).\n\n**Tenure** \u2014 `Membership.pointsOf` now grants the +3 tenure points based on `FiscalYears.elapsedSinceRegistration(owner) > 1` (elapsed fiscal years) rather than a 365-day window; removed the old `tenureDays`/`ChronoUnit` code. New owners still have zero tenure, keeping the level cap (Cp39/Cp40).\n\nDescriptions in `openapi.yml` were updated to match the new fiscal-year semantics. With today (2026-08-16, a Sunday) rolling to Monday 2026-08-17, owners correctly report `FY27` / `-M27`.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 60, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
